name 'Card Sort Game'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
<!-- Internet Card Sort: Misconceptions vs. True Concepts -->
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 20px; width: 95%; margin: 20px auto;">

  <!-- Column 1: Card Statements -->
  <div style="background-color: #F7F8FA; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">🧠 Sort These Statements</p>
    <ul style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 2; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>WiFi and the Internet are the same thing.</li>
<br>
      <li>The Internet is one big computer that everyone connects to.</li>
<br>
      <li>The Web is the Internet (they're just different names).</li>
      <li>Data travels in a straight line from my device to the website.</li>
      <li>Once a message is sent, it can't be broken into smaller pieces.</li>
      <li>If one router fails, the whole Internet goes down.</li>
      <li>An IP address is just a username, like an email handle.</li>
      <li>DNS is where all websites are stored.</li>
      <li>HTTP is only used when you submit a form.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; color: #292F36;">Think about which are true and which are common misconceptions before revealing the answers.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 2: Reveal the Correct Sort -->
  <div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; padding: 20px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">✅ Correct Sort</p>
    <details style="margin-bottom: 15px;">
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">❌ Misconceptions</summary>
      <ul style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 10px;">
        <li>WiFi and the Internet are the same thing.</li>
        <li>The Internet is one big computer that everyone connects to.</li>
        <li>The Web is the Internet (they're just different names).</li>
        <li>Data travels in a straight line from my device to the website.</li>
        <li>Once a message is sent, it can't be broken into smaller pieces.</li>
        <li>If one router fails, the whole Internet goes down.</li>
        <li>An IP address is just a username, like an email handle.</li>
        <li>DNS is where all websites are stored.</li>
        <li>HTTP is only used when you submit a form.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer;">✅ True Concepts</summary>
      <ul style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 10px;">
        <li>None of the statements above are fully accurate.</li>
        <li>Each reflects a common misunderstanding that can be clarified through discussion.</li>
        <li>This card sort helps surface misconceptions and build clearer mental models! 💡</li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </div>

</div>

<details>
  <summary>Click me</summary>
  <p>This is hidden until clicked.</p>
</details>
MARKDOWN
